  "body_html": "<h1>Semi-Reduced Normal Form</h1>\n<p>Two strategies $s_i,t_i$ of player $i$ are payoff-equivalent if for every\n$s_{-i}$ and every player $j$,\n$$\n  g_j(s_i,s_{-i})=g_j(t_i,s_{-i}).\n$$\nThe semi-reduced normal form identifies payoff-equivalent strategies. This removes\ndifferences that occur only at positions excluded by the strategy itself.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 6.2.3] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>, <code>references/MathFoundationsGameTheory.pdf</code>. Semi-reduced normal form identifies payoff-equivalent strategies.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
